{
 "note": "Mutants of the block of docker/nginx.conf that passes GET /lobbies (the public list of games, docs/SERVER.md 'Lobby rooms') for tools/mutate.py (docs/WORKFLOW.md, 'Mutation checks'). Run from the checkout with the program nginx installed: python3 tools/mutate.py tests/data/nginx_lobbies_mutants.json --keep-going --jobs 1. Every mutant must be caught by tests/scripts/test_nginx_lobbies.py: each breaks one rule of the block - the method and the query, the exact location, the one path that goes on, what is passed on, the cache (two seconds, one entry for everybody, only a 200), the old answer (only while a new one is fetched, never for an error or a hang-up; for a server that hangs, the read timeout of three seconds), the allowance (a hundred a second, a burst of two hundred, its own zone, the address of the connection as its key) and the fallback (404, the JSON word, its type and no-store). The mutants change docker/nginx.conf only, and put it back.",
 "defaults": {
  "test": "python3 tests/scripts/test_nginx_lobbies.py -f"
 },
